From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:05:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: ucode: don't crash on a BSS that is gone in
 set_bss_order

iface.set_bss_order() takes the hostapd_data of each listed BSS from its
ucode resource and dereferences it without a check. A resource whose BSS
hostapd has already freed holds no data, and hostapd dies with SIGSEGV.

Seen on an OpenWrt One (mt76) on 2026-11-10: a reload of a configuration
whose only change was the radios' txpower took iface_reload_config()'s
BSS path for phy1, and all four BSS resources in the list it passed to
set_bss_order() were already empty (read from the core dump). hostapd
died and took every BSS on both radios with it, until netifd restarted
Wi-Fi 30 seconds later.

Treat such an entry like any other one that does not belong to the
interface: return null. The reload then logs "Failed to update BSS
order" and restarts that phy's interface, and the other radio keeps
running.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=hostapd
-PKG_RELEASE:=18
+PKG_RELEASE:=19
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://w1.fi/hostap.git
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ucode.c
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ucode.c
@@ -622,7 +622,7 @@ uc_hostapd_iface_set_bss_order(uc_vm_t *
 		struct hostapd_data *bss;
 
 		bss = ucv_resource_data(ucv_array_get(bss_list, i), "hostapd.bss");
-		if (bss->iface != iface)
+		if (!bss || bss->iface != iface)
 			goto free;
 
 		for (size_t k = 0; k < i; k++)
